= Training set — Simple =

A '''training set''' is the data a machine-learning system uses to learn.

The learning algorithm changes the model based on these examples.

Training data are different from validation data, which help choose settings, and test data, which are saved for final evaluation.

There is no rule that training data must always be exactly 70%, 80%, or any other fixed percentage.

